# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# Without this the working tree is MIXED: `core.autocrlf` is true in the system
# gitconfig and false in this repo, so files land differently depending on when
# and how they were checked out. That is not cosmetic. ADR-041 pinned SHA-256
# digests of the committed history entries -- the anchor every arm-scoping check
# rests on -- and the pins were taken from a mixed tree: one entry LF, two CRLF,
# against three pure-LF blobs. No uniform checkout could satisfy all three, so
# CI would have failed on an honest tree and accused the PR of rewriting
# append-only history. Found by the Platform Engineering seat.
#
# The digest itself now normalises, so it no longer depends on this. This exists
# so the NEXT byte-level check does not have to rediscover it, and so a diff
# stops showing every line of a file as changed when only three were.
* text=auto eol=lf
